    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the read-only `telephoneDisplay` field, which returns the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans while leaving the raw `telephone` field as canonical E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added a `toDisplay(String e164)` method (plus a small `groupInThrees` helper). It splits off the country code using the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` table (longest-code-first, consistent with normalization), then emits `\"+\" + countryCode + \" \" + <national digits grouped in threes>`. Unknown country codes fall back to grouping the whole digit run in threes, and `null` passes through.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the new field in with `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", ...)` and a `@Named(\"formatTelephoneDisplay\")` method delegating to `TelephoneNormalizer.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, following the same `qualifiedByName` pattern used by the other derived fields.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (input `0412 345 678` \u2192 `telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full build is green.",
